model_contract.prompt:
Inspect only the single supplied image. Detect visible indoor furniture from exactly these categories: chair, table, sofa, cabinet, bed, shelf. A desk is table; a couch is sofa; a bookcase is shelf. Do not infer hidden objects or use prior images. Return all visibly identifiable instances of those categories. For a partly occluded object, bound only its visible image extent. If the picture is too dark, blurred or otherwise unusable for judging furniture, set quality_usable to false. Return ONLY a JSON object, with no markdown or explanation, in this format:
{"quality_usable":true,"objects":[{"category":"chair","bbox":[100,200,300,400]}]}
Each bbox is [left,top,right,bottom] in PIXELS of the supplied image, with origin at the image top-left. Use left<right and top<bottom. The exact supplied image width and height follow. If no listed furniture is visibly identifiable, return an empty objects array. Do not report risk, safety, object identities or probabilities.
